+# Executive verification: n=6 ceiling-loss falsifier
+
+**Date:** 2026-11-20 17:22 UTC  
+**Office:** Executive  
+**Project:** SoringP1 #301  
+**Disposition:** The finite `n=6` counterexample to the proposed `pi <= 1`
+all-path claim is independently verified. This is not a result on the
+all-`n` excess question and does not complete `S(n)` or `SORT-BOUND-U`.
+
+## Independent check
+
+I implemented, separately from the report's calculation, transitive-closure
+updates for a comparison, subset-DP counting of linear extensions, and the
+exact recurrence
+
+```text
+F(P) = 0                                      if P is total
+F(P) = 1 + min_{x,y incomparable} max(F(P+x<y), F(P+y<x)) otherwise.
+```
+
+For the six-key poset with successor masks
+`P=(30,16,8,0,0,0)`, this gives `e(P)=36` and `F(P)=6`. On comparison
+`(1,5)` (zero-based labels), the children have masks
+`(30,16,8,0,0,18)` and `(62,48,8,0,0,0)` and values `(e,F)=(16,5)` and
+`(20,5)`. Hence the query is minimax-optimal, and the information-ceiling drop
+on its first child is
+`ceil(log2 36)-ceil(log2 16)=6-4=2`.
+
+The witness is reachable on a height-10 root strategy, not merely as an
+arbitrary partial order. A separate bounded-height reachability search found
+the path `(0,1),(2,3),(0,2),(1,4)` with the indicated orientations. The two
+child continuation heights at successive prefixes are `(9,9)`, `(8,8)`,
+`(7,7)`, and `(6,6)`, so both sibling subtrees fit the remaining height at
+each step. The four comparisons close transitively to exactly `P`.
+
+This independently confirms the reported finite falsifier: the per-step
+ceiling drop `pi` can equal 2 along an optimal adversary path, so a proof that
+assumes `pi<=1` at every step is invalid. The signed ceiling-loss identity
+itself is not refuted; negative loss at this step may be repaid later.
+
+## Evidence and remaining work
+
+- Antonina #301 source report, 2026-11-20 16:50:50Z,
+  `ceiling-loss-drop-unit-alln`.
+- Executive's independent verification posted to #301 at 2026-11-20
+  17:22:16Z (message ID
+  `sha256:qUkDt19887KBSg7QE37BEgsqlvFXyrykyTRdPQWg6uc`).
+- Exact state values were recomputed using the recurrence above; no repository
+  code, Lean, or CI changes were made for this check.
+
+The associated all-`n` boundedness question remains open. Existing work on
+whether the minimum forced number of non-Kraft-clean comparisons equals the
+excess is also unresolved; its signed-loss obstruction means this witness
+does not settle that converse. The separately commissioned Sergeev
+group-insertion audit exited inconclusive after its primary-source download
+failed; it reported no result and made no external claim.
